.SH NAME
maknoon-session-derive - Derive a session key from a passphrase and print it as hex


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmaknoon session derive [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Derives a 32-byte AES key from a passphrase using Argon2id and prints it as hex.
Use the output with --session-key on subsequent encrypt/decrypt calls to skip
the per-file KDF cost (~26ms per file) when processing many files.

.PP
Example:
  KEY=$(maknoon session derive -s mypassphrase)
  maknoon encrypt --session-key "$KEY" file1.txt
  maknoon encrypt --session-key "$KEY" file2.txt


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for derive

.PP
\fB-s\fP, \fB--passphrase\fP=""
	Passphrase to derive from


